# QDEF Standard Record Type Registry
#
# This file is the canonical, machine-readable field registry for the
# spec's own standard Record Types (QDEF-SPEC.md §4) -- the low
# TypeId range 1-22, Standards Action governed. It is written in the
# GNU recfile format, same as registry.rec, so tooling can build
# STANDARD_TYPE_NAMES / STANDARD_SHAPES from it directly instead of
# duplicating the shape data by hand in assets/cbor-util.js.
#
# Unlike registry.rec (community namespaces, open to PRs from anyone --
# see the First Come First Served tier, §3.5/§3.6), every entry here is
# Governance: standards-action -- changes go through the spec itself
# (QDEF-SPEC.md §4), not a standalone registration PR. Bundle (§4.6)
# carries no TypeId and no fixed field shape, so it has no entry below;
# it stays documented in the spec prose only.

%rec: StandardType
%mandatory: TypeId RecordTypeName Governance
%sort: TypeId

TypeId: 1
RecordTypeName: Split
Section: 4.1
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 0: bstr (Fragment Bytes), 2: bstr (Group ID), 4: uint (Fragment Index), 6: uint (Fragment Count), 7: uint (Total Bytes, opt), 9: uint (Parity Scheme, opt) }
Semantics: Fragment reassembly across a multi-code group, with optional XOR parity recovery.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#41-wrapper-records-optional

TypeId: 2
RecordTypeName: Encrypt
Section: 4.1
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 0: bstr (Ciphertext + Tag), 2: bstr (Nonce), 3: uint or tstr (Algorithm, opt), 5: uint or tstr (Key Algorithm, opt) }
Semantics: AEAD wrapper (e.g. AES-256-GCM); algorithm fields borrow the COSE Algorithm ID registry.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#41-wrapper-records-optional

TypeId: 3
RecordTypeName: Media Payload
Section: 4.3
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 0: bstr (Content), 1: uint or tstr (Media Type, opt) }
Semantics: Typed binary content; media_type is a CoAP Content-Format ID or a literal MIME string.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#43-media-payload-optional

TypeId: 4
RecordTypeName: Compress
Section: 4.1
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 0: bstr (Deflated Bytes) }
Semantics: DEFLATE wrapper.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#41-wrapper-records-optional

TypeId: 5
RecordTypeName: Open/Hint URI
Section: 4.2
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 0: tstr (URI), 1: tstr (Label, opt), 3: tstr (Language, opt), 5: uint (Action, opt) }
Semantics: URI a generic tool can open; fallback/hint for containers with richer content.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#42-openhint-uri-optional

TypeId: 6
RecordTypeName: App Route
Section: 4.4
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 0: tstr or bstr (Origin), 1: tstr (Hint Name, opt) }
Semantics: Application dispatch by verified domain or hash-derived name.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#44-app-route-optional

TypeId: 7
RecordTypeName: Media Preview
Section: 4.5
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 2: uint or tstr (Media Type), 3: bstr (Content Hash, opt), 5: tstr (Filename, opt), 7: tstr (Label, opt) }
Semantics: Content identification (media type, multihash-style hash, filename, label) independent of the payload bytes, which travel as a subrecord.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#45-media-preview-optional

TypeId: 8
RecordTypeName: Signature
Section: 4.7
Governance: standards-action
DataItem: map { 0: bstr (Signature), 2: nint (Algorithm), 4: bstr (Public Key) }
Semantics: Detached authenticity over the Records immediately preceding it in the same array.
Reference: docs/QDEF-SPEC.md#47-signature-optional
